sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant NATS as NATS JetStream
    participant Worker as Worker
    participant DB as PostgreSQL inbox + execution + outbox
    participant Target as Effect destination

    NATS->>Worker: Deliver event, at least once
    Worker->>DB: Begin transaction and insert inbox key

    alt Worker crashes before commit
        Note over DB: Transaction rolls back. No inbox key or execution persists.
        NATS->>Worker: Redeliver event after ack wait of 30s
        Worker->>DB: Process as new event
    else Commit succeeds but worker crashes before ACK
        Worker->>DB: Commit inbox, execution and outbox together
        NATS->>Worker: Redeliver event
        Worker->>DB: Find committed inbox key
        DB-->>Worker: Existing execution
        Worker->>NATS: Ack without creating a second execution
    end

    Worker->>DB: Claim outbox effect with SKIP LOCKED
    Worker->>Target: Send effect with deterministic effect ID
    Note over Target: Destination treats effect ID as an idempotency key.

    Note over NATS,Target: Result, at-least-once transport becomes one business execution<br/>and safely repeatable effect delivery.
